oduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:efb796051150338c245710906b5d04d9e8c17174637d1f50a5022a14fbc431a3","file":"preprints/Disk-transfer-representations-and-confined-bridge-mass-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":80,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"aca711841f96dfdb7083986640857d36743e1c0b1b192155ca4948abf93312a3","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Disk-transfer-representations-and-confined-bridge-mass-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:efb796051150338c245710906b5d04d9e8c17174637d1f50a5022a14fbc431a3","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Disk-transfer-representations-and-confined-bridge-mass-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L80"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:boundary}\\label{c2:thm-annealed}\nThe following conclusions hold as the indicated scale tends to infinity.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item The arch kernel is nonincreasing and\n\\[\n h(m)\\asymp m^{-5/4},\\qquad\n \\mu(\\operatorname{height}>R)\\asymp\n \\mu(\\operatorname{diameter}>R)\\asymp R^{-1/4}.\n\\]\n\\item For every sufficiently large fixed $C$, normalize $\\mu$ either on\n$R\\le\\operatorname{diameter}\\le CR$, or on\n$\\operatorname{height}\\ge R$ and $\\operatorname{diameter}\\le CR$.\nUnder either law, $\\mathbb E\\ell=R^{4/3+o(1)}$.\n\\item Let\n\\[\n D_R=\\{y:e_i\\cdot y<R,\\ i=0,1,2\\},\\qquad\n I_R=\\{v\\text{ a lattice vertex}:e_i\\cdot v<(1-\\varepsilon)R,\n \\ i=0,1,2\\},\n\\]\nwhere $R\\in\\frac12+\\frac32\\mathbb Z$ and $\\varepsilon>0$ is sufficiently\nsmall and fixed.  Sum critical chord weights over the ordered pair of\nboundary ports and normalize on chords visiting $I_R$.\nUniformly for $v\\in I_R$, their visit probability is $R^{-2/3+o(1)}$.\nThe expected total number of visited vertices, and the expected number in\n$I_R$, are both $R^{4/3+o(1)}$.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
